        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Pomphet",
        "main_title": "The best hotels in Ayutthaya",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "A laid-back riverside stay in Ayutthaya with views of ancient ruins and temples. Interiors blend warm wood tones with clean, modern lines. There’s a pool, gym, cruise tours, and a Thai restaurant with serious style. Great spot for a quiet break with just enough to do.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Cycling - Rent a bike to pedal through emerald rice paddies and centuries‑old temple grounds, pausing to photograph the iconic Buddha‑head",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Local markets - Browse vibrant stalls at Chao Phrom Market before noon, savouring boat noodles, Thai sweets, and the hum of local daily life",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Short break - Perfect for a quick escape - lounge in lush gardens, dine riverside, then cruise past Ayutthaya’s glowing sunset ruins",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Other Activities - Glide along the Chao Phraya at sunset aboard a private long‑tail, admiring sunset hues dancing over ancient temples",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
